{
  "_README": "Need-state classification eval set — 150 labeled inputs across 3 languages (English, Spanish w/ Catalan code-mix, German w/ English code-mix). This is the 150-input pilot the PRD lists as a companion artifact (PRD §6.1). Hard cases (sarcasm, understatement, mixed states, idioms that must NOT trigger crisis, indirect crisis phrasing) are oversampled. In the real product this would expand to 1,000+ inputs labeled by >=2 raters with inter-rater agreement reported per need-state.",
  "schema": {
    "id": "stable id",
    "text": "the user input",
    "language": "en | es | de",
    "code_mixed": "true if it mixes languages (es+Catalan, de+English)",
    "need_state": "distract | validate | calm | energize | company | crisis",
    "is_crisis": "true only for genuine self-harm/suicidal-intent inputs",
    "crisis_tier": "none | soft | hard  (expected output of the independent crisis classifier)",
    "hard_case": "none | sarcasm | understatement | mixed | idiom | indirect"
  },
  "labeling_notes": "Single-author labels for this pilot (portfolio artifact); production requires >=2 independent raters + adjudication. 'mixed' = competing needs where the dominant ACTIONABLE need wins (e.g. sad + must work -> distract). 'idiom' items use figures of speech ('killing me', 'dying of boredom') and MUST stay crisis_tier=none — they test crisis precision. 'soft' items are heavy but ambiguous distress: resources shown alongside a recommendation, never instead.",
  "items": [
